<section class="about" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
	<h2 class="about-title" id="about-title">About</h2>
	<div class="about-copy">
		<p>Ukrainian graphic designer and visual artist studying at the Royal Academy of Fine Arts Antwerp.</p>
		<p class="small">
			Hi, I'm Ksusha, a Ukrainian graphic designer and visual artist studying Master at the Royal Academy of Fine Arts Antwerp.
			<!-- My practice moves between graphic design, typography, publications, illustration, ceramics and spatial objects. I
			collect overlooked details and use making as a way to ask questions. I am interested in collaborations, commissions
			and internships. -->
		</p>
		<p class="small">I'm not very good at choosing one medium and staying with it.</p>
		<p class="small">I make books, illustrations, ceramics, typography and objects. Sometimes I begin with a drawing and end up building a letter almost as tall as me. Sometimes I collect random fragments for weeks without knowing what they will become.</p>
		<p class="small">I'm attracted to things that are slightly strange, imperfect or easy to miss: awkward shapes, handwritten signs, unusual packaging, broken compositions, accidental colour combinations and objects that seem to have their own personality.</p>
		<p class="small">Most of my work begins with curiosity rather than a clear plan. I like touching materials, moving things around, making mistakes and seeing where they take me. I'm probably more interested in the moment when an idea changes than in following the original plan perfectly.</p>
		<p class="small">This account is a mixture of finished projects, unfinished experiments, things I notice and things I'm still trying to understand.
			At the moment, I'm open to collaborations, commissions, internships and unexpected ideas.</p>
		<p class="small">So, hi. This is what I make - or at least some of it.</p>
	</div>
</section>

